From: Honor 6X local port <honor6x-local@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 22:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: do not start, stop, or delete external P2P devices

The Honor 6X vendor driver pre-creates p2p0, but its
start_p2p_device callback is an unimplemented stub that always returns an
error. The stop callback is also a stub. An externally owned P2P Device must
therefore not use the generic nl80211 lifecycle managed by wpa_supplicant.

Leave start, stop, and deletion to the vendor driver while retaining the
normal lifecycle for P2P Devices created by wpa_supplicant itself.
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
index 945ba6f..c1b73ea 100644
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -3041,7 +3041,10 @@ wpa_driver_nl80211_finish_drv_init(struct wpa_driver_nl80211_data *drv,
 	wpa_driver_nl80211_drv_init_rfkill(drv);
 
 	if (!rfkill_is_blocked(drv->rfkill)) {
-		int ret = i802_set_iface_flags(bss, 1);
+		int ret = 0;
+
+		if (!bss->externally_owned_p2p_device)
+			ret = i802_set_iface_flags(bss, 1);
 		if (ret) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "nl80211: Could not set "
 				   "interface '%s' UP", bss->ifname);
@@ -3204,7 +3207,8 @@ static void wpa_driver_nl80211_deinit(struct i802_bss *bss)
 
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv, drv->ctx);
 
-	if (!drv->start_iface_up)
+	if (!drv->start_iface_up &&
+	    !bss->externally_owned_p2p_device)
 		(void) i802_set_iface_flags(bss, 0);
 
 	if (drv->addr_changed) {
-- 
